  "notes": "Godan verb ({五段動詞|ごだんどうし}), む-ending.\n- Negative: {澄|す}まない\n- Polite: {澄|す}みます\n- Te-form: {澄|す}んで\n- Past: {澄|す}んだ\n\nUSAGE:\nOften used in the て⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ form ({澄|す}んで⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧) to describe a state of clarity. The compound {澄|す}みわたる means \"to be perfectly clear throughout.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{水|みず}→水：02258_mizu⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{澄|す}む: the water becomes clear\n- ⟦{空気|くうき}→空気：01390_kuuki⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{澄|す}む: the air becomes clear\n- {澄|す}んだ⟦{目|め}→目：00525_me⟧: clear eyes\n- {澄|す}んだ⟦{声|こえ}→声：02207_koe⟧: a clear voice\n- {澄|す}みわたる: to be perfectly clear",
